WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.167
Look from one eye

2
00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.933
to the other in a mirror.

3
00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:04.100
Why can't you normally

4
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:04.967
catch the movement?

5
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.600
Now record your eyes,

6
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.900
and watch it back.

7
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.867
There it is.

8
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.367
Each quick jump

9
00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:11.533
is a saccade.

10
00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:12.733
In the mirror,

11
00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:14.033
the eyes you're watching

12
00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.300
are also the eyes

13
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.267
doing the looking.

14
00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:17.733
As they turn,

15
00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:18.900
the image sweeps

16
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.100
across the retina.

17
00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.033
Visual sensitivity drops

18
00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.667
around the movement.

19
00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.333
That's saccadic suppression.

20
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.633
The clear views

21
00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:27.700
before and after

22
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.733
can also mask

23
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:29.767
the brief blur.

24
00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.833
You aren't completely blind.

25
00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.133
These effects help

26
00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.467
keep vision stable.

27
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:36.300
Watching a recording later

28
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.433
separates the movement

29
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:39.400
from your own eye turn.

30
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.167
The mirror never stopped

31
00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:41.867
showing it.

32
00:00:41.867 --> 00:00:43.333
Your visual system normally

33
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:44.400
keeps the sweep

34
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.500
out of awareness.
